The interface and verification configuration adapt crypto/pq/mldsa44.cpp and
mldsa44-config.h from tosnetwork/tos at
8f083dc06bff16705710a01de15eb3123d5d696b. On 2026-10-10, RTOS implemented the
Rust FFI boundary and changed the configuration's native symbol namespace.

native/mldsa-native contains an unmodified copy of that revision's vendored
mldsa compilation subtree and license files. Its declared upstream version is
mldsa-native v2.0.0, commit 834a90d5e846ffa1e1611bd24e160bb2e9b86d35.
Copyright (c) The mldsa-native project authors.
Apache-2.0 OR ISC OR MIT; see native/mldsa-native/LICENSE and RELICENSE.md.

The public OpenSSL fixtures are copied from the reference's
 test/pq-mldsa44/fixtures.json; its GPLv3 text is tests/data/TOS-LICENSE.txt.

RTOS acknowledges the National Institute of Standards and Technology as the
source of the ACVP vectors (ACVP-Server commit
975de31eb83d87039ec88934fdc47d8c312b892d). On 2026-10-10, RTOS extracted the
pure ML-DSA-44 external-interface cases into TSV and classified inputs outside
the bounded verification profile as malformed. The entire original NIST
notice is retained in tests/data/ACVP-LICENSE.txt.

Wycheproof vectors are from C2SP/wycheproof commit
3fa63dd0344abb611f1fb1d77e119938603ea230, under Apache-2.0; see
 tests/data/WYCHEPROOF-LICENSE.txt. Vector values and verdicts are preserved
except for explicit malformed-input classification at the Rust API's bounds.

The context-binding fixture uses a public deterministic test seed. It was
created with the same native backend and is not an independent crypto reference.
Detailed import hashes, corpus generation and test evidence are maintained at
https://github.com/tosnetwork/memo/tree/main/rtos.
